  "before_interfaces": {
    "lem-hh-tensor-algebra-regular-detection": [
      "## Statement\n\nLet $A$ be a unital algebra over a field $k$. For $n=2,3$, give $A^{\\otimes n}$ its iterated componentwise tensor-product algebra structure and unit $1_A^{\\otimes n}$. If $X,Y\\in A^{\\otimes n}$ and left multiplication by $X$ and $Y$ agree as maps $A^{\\otimes n}\\to A^{\\otimes n}$, then $X=Y$. In particular, evaluation of a left-multiplication operator at $1_A^{\\otimes n}$ recovers the tensor that defines it."
    ],
    "def-hh-leg-notation-and-quasitriangular-hopf-algebra": [
      "## Definition\n\nSet $H^{\\otimes3}:=(H\\otimes H)\\otimes H$. Define linear maps\n$\\iota_{12}(a\\otimes b)=(a\\otimes b)\\otimes1_H,\\qquad \\iota_{13}(a\\otimes b)=(a\\otimes1_H)\\otimes b,\\qquad \\iota_{23}(a\\otimes b)=(1_H\\otimes a)\\otimes b.$\nFor $X\\in H\\otimes H$, write $X_{ij}:=\\iota_{ij}(X)$ and $X_{21}:=\\tau_{H,H}(X)$, where $\\tau_{H,H}(a\\otimes b)=b\\otimes a$. Define $\\Delta^{\\mathrm{op}}:=\\tau_{H,H}\\circ\\Delta$. In the second hexagon below, $\\alpha^{-1}_{H,H,H}$ is the canonical reassociation $(H\\otimes(H\\otimes H))\\to((H\\otimes H)\\otimes H)$ from [F4].\n\nAn algebraic quasitriangular structure on $H$ is an invertible element $R\\in H\\otimes H$ such that, for every $h\\in H$,\n$R\\Delta(h)=\\Delta^{\\mathrm{op}}(h)R,$\nand\n$(\\Delta\\otimes\\operatorname{id}_H)(R)=R_{13}R_{23},\\qquad \\alpha^{-1}_{H,H,H}(\\operatorname{id}_H\\otimes\\Delta)(R)=R_{13}R_{12}.$\nAll products are in the componentwise tensor-product algebra, and $R$ is a finite algebraic tensor sum. The displayed formula with $\\alpha^{-1}$ is the parenthesized form of $(\\operatorname{id}\\otimes\\Delta)R=R_{13}R_{12}$."
    ],
    "lem-hh-quasitriangular-counit-and-yang-baxter-identities": [
      "## Statement\n\nLet $H$ be a Hopf algebra over a field $k$ and let $R\\in H\\otimes H$ be invertible and satisfy the quasitriangular axioms of [[def-hh-leg-notation-and-quasitriangular-hopf-algebra]]. Then\n$(\\varepsilon\\otimes\\operatorname{id})(R)=1_H=(\\operatorname{id}\\otimes\\varepsilon)(R),$\nand\n$R_{12}R_{13}R_{23}=R_{23}R_{13}R_{12}\\quad\\text{in }H^{\\otimes3}.$"
    ],
    "def-hh-braiding-and-triangular-structure": [
      "## Definition\n\nLet $H$ be a Hopf algebra over a field $k$ and let $H\\text{-Mod}$ denote the category of all left $H$-modules and all $H$-linear maps, with tensor action and associators as in [[def-hh-module-category-and-tensor-action]] and [[thm-hh-bialgebra-module-tensor-coherence]]. A braiding on this category is a family of $H$-linear isomorphisms\n$c_{V,W}:V\\otimes W\\longrightarrow W\\otimes V$\nfor all left $H$-modules $V,W$, natural in both variables, for which the following equalities hold after inserting the canonical associators of the module category:\n$c_{U,V\\otimes W}=(\\operatorname{id}_V\\otimes c_{U,W})\\circ(c_{U,V}\\otimes\\operatorname{id}_W),\\qquad c_{U\\otimes V,W}=(c_{U,W}\\otimes\\operatorname{id}_V)\\circ(\\operatorname{id}_U\\otimes c_{V,W}).$\nA quasitriangular structure $R$ is triangular if $R_{21}R=1_H\\otimes1_H$. A braiding is symmetric if $c_{W,V}\\circ c_{V,W}=\\operatorname{id}_{V\\otimes W}$ for every $V,W$. No finite-dimensional restriction is imposed on $H$ or on the modules in $H\\text{-Mod}$."
    ],
    "thm-hh-r-matrix-constructs-a-module-braiding": [
      "## Statement\n\nLet $H$ be a Hopf algebra over a field $k$ and let $R\\in H\\otimes H$ be an algebraic quasitriangular structure. For any left $H$-modules $V,W$, define\n$c_{V,W}(v\\otimes w)=\\tau_{V,W}\\big((\\rho_V\\otimes\\rho_W)(R)(v\\otimes w)\\big)=\\sum_i b_iw\\otimes a_iv$\nwhen $R=\\sum_i a_i\\otimes b_i$. These maps form a braiding on the category of **all** left $H$-modules. The associated operator $\\check R_V=c_{V,V}$ satisfies the Yang–Baxter braid relation on $V^{\\otimes3}$. The braiding is symmetric exactly when $R_{21}R=1\\otimes1$. Conversely, every braiding on the category of all left $H$-modules uniquely determines an algebraic quasitriangular element $R\\in H\\otimes H$ by\n$R=\\tau_{H,H}\\big(c_{H,H}(1_H\\otimes1_H)\\big).$\nThis converse uses naturality on all modules, including the regular module $H$, and does not assume finite dimensionality."
    ],
    "lem-hh-local-braiding-operators-obey-braid-relations": [
      "## Statement\n\nLet $V$ be a left module over a quasitriangular Hopf algebra and let $n\\ge2$. Set $\\check R:=c_{V,V}$, with $c$ as in [[thm-hh-r-matrix-constructs-a-module-braiding]]. For $1\\le i<n$, let $T_i$ be the operator on $V^{\\otimes n}$ that acts by $\\check R$ on tensor positions $i,i+1$ and by the identity on every other position, using the canonical associators of [[lem-hh-tensor-coherence-on-elementary-tensors]]. Then\n$T_iT_{i+1}T_i=T_{i+1}T_iT_{i+1}\\quad(1\\le i<n-1),\\qquad T_iT_j=T_jT_i\\quad(|i-j|>1).$\nThese relations are the local operator facts used by later Hecke constructions; no quadratic relation is asserted."
    ],
